{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "7ca8a1e7-06f7-4f60-8f95-8b5c6b5c8b2f",
    "name": "Todo List API - Todo Controller",
    "description": "Import this collection and local.postman_environment.json, then select Todo List API - Local.\n\n1. Start the Users API (http://localhost:5001) and Todo API (http://localhost:5002).\n2. Set userName and userPass in the selected environment to an existing active user's credentials.\n3. Send Login - Users API. It saves token.accessToken as todo_bearer_token and accessToken, plus the returned userId.\n4. Send a Todo request. Each request has an explicit Authorization: Bearer {{todo_bearer_token}} header. The authorization helper is disabled to keep one Authorization header.\n\nFor a manually obtained token, set todo_bearer_token to the raw token.accessToken string and send a Todo request directly. The accessToken variable is also accepted, and an optional pasted Bearer prefix is removed. Missing, malformed, expired, or mismatched JWTs are stopped with a diagnostic before sending the Todo request. The API validates the signature.\n\nJWT configuration: this API requires Jwt:Audience = portfolio-todo-rest-api. The Users API must include portfolio-todo-rest-api in Jwt:Audiences. Restart the Users API after changing JWT settings and log in again to obtain a token with the updated audience list. Adding the header alone cannot repair an existing token's audience. jwt_issuer and jwt_audience describe the expected server settings for diagnostics; changing these Postman variables does not change server configuration.\n\nA full collection run creates, reads, updates, and deletes one sample todo. categoryId must reference an existing category; the default 1001 is supplied by the optional category seed script.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "noauth"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Login - Users API",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const userName = String(pm.variables.get('userName') || '').trim();",
              "const userPass = String(pm.variables.get('userPass') || '');",
              "if (!userName || !userPass) {",
              "    const message = 'Select Todo List API - Local and set userName and userPass before sending Login - Users API. To use an existing token, send a Todo request directly.';",
              "    pm.test('Login credentials are configured', function () {",
              "        pm.expect.fail(message);",
              "    });",
              "    console.error(message);",
              "    pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "}",
              "pm.environment.set('todo_bearer_token', '');",
              "pm.environment.set('accessToken', '');",
              "pm.variables.unset('todo_bearer_token');",
              "pm.variables.unset('accessToken');",
              "pm.request.body.update(JSON.stringify({ userName: userName, userPass: userPass }));"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Login status code is 200', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    pm.test('Login returns an access token and user ID', function () {",
              "        const body = pm.response.json();",
              "        pm.expect(body.token).to.be.an('object');",
              "        pm.expect(body.token.accessToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
              "        pm.expect(body.userId).to.be.a('number').and.above(0);",
              "        pm.environment.set('todo_bearer_token', body.token.accessToken);",
              "        pm.environment.set('accessToken', body.token.accessToken);",
              "        pm.environment.set('userId', body.userId);",
              "        pm.variables.set('todo_bearer_token', body.token.accessToken);",
              "    });",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "auth": {
          "type": "noauth"
        },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"userName\": \"{{userName}}\",\n  \"userPass\": \"{{userPass}}\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": "{{users_base_url}}/api/auth/login",
        "description": "Authenticate with the separate Users API. Supply userName and userPass in the selected environment. The response script saves token.accessToken and userId for the Todo requests. Re-run this request after fixing the Users API JWT audiences or when the token expires."
      },
      "response": []
